        <div class="lp-prose">
          <p>Chicago's two-flats, greystones, and bungalows in zip codes {zipCodes} — Lincoln Park, Logan Square, Wicker Park, Hyde Park, Pilsen, Old Town — are built from Chicago Common brick and limestone greystone, both requiring lime-based mortar. Portland cement applied over Chicago Common brick is the single most common damage pattern we correct: it traps moisture, spalls the brick face, and can cause irreversible damage to irreplaceable material.</p>
          <p>Greystones need even softer mortar than brick — standard tuckpointing compounds destroy the limestone surface. Courtyard buildings often have decades of mismatched repair history we assess elevation-by-elevation before any work starts. Free estimates, written scope, and licensed tuckpointing and brick repair across Cook County since 2007. No Portland cement on Chicago Common brick — ever.</p>
